{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "CRUD in Web Development "}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talking about web development."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "\"Uses the four basic functions in persistent storage to create the system.   Talks about the four basic functions for persistent storage. \""}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on persisting storage, web applications, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Be Going To"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use be <b>going to</b> to express future ideas."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You're going to see that it is pretty similar to REST."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Today, we're going to talk about CRUD in web development"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<b><i>Going to</b></i> is somehow similar to <i>will</i> as they both work to express future ideas, but there are some differences.</br></br>You use <b>be going to</b> to express future ideas that were planned before the moment of speaking.</br></br>Check the following example:</br><i>Today, we <b>are going to</b> talk about web development.</i></br></br>In the previous example, the speaker planned talking about web development beforehand. Therefore, the idea is expressed with <b>be going to</b> rather than <b>will</b>.</br></br>In order to make a sentence using <b>be going to</b>, you use the following structure:</br></br><center>Subject + <b>verb 'to be'</b> + <b>going to</b> + <b>action verb in its base form</b> + complement.</center></br>For example:</br><i>You <b>are going to learn</b> the differences between CRUD and REST. </br>She <b>is going to program</b> some PHP files to make a CRUD.</i></br></br>Keep in mind that you can contract the verb \u2018to be' with the subject."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "CRUD and Web Development"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about web development, <b>CRUD</b> is the same as REST."}, {"type": "text", "content": "REST is the short form of Representational State Transfer, which can be seen as a protocol to communicate and send instructions to webpages through HTTP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Such instructions are related to the CRUD functions in a database, but in the web development field REST is considered as a superset of CRUD since all components of CRUD are embedded in REST but not the other way around. Thus, REST contains the same Create, Read, Update and Delete functions but with other terminology, which are Post, Get, Delete, Put and Patch among others."}, {"type": "text", "content": "As an overall, the use of CRUD or REST in web development is to send commands to webpages so that some processes take place, such as retrieving the geolocation or a picture from a web page or application, or to simply make a post or deleting one you have previously done."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "development "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the creation process of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now, you ought to understand that such commands will work differently in web development."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stand for "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to represent, as in a group of letters"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sorry, teacher. What does it stand for?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "API "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Application Programming Interface; a way to communicate with a computer or internet service"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(acronym)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is an API that, in short, helps clients to exchange data with the servers via HTTP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in short "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "briefly explained "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is an API that, in short, helps clients to exchange data with the servers via HTTP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "HTTP"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Hypertext Transfer Protocol: instructions made by a program to connect computers with internet documents"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is an API that, in short, helps clients to exchange data with the servers via HTTP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "jargon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "specialized language and terms used in specific contexts"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Guys, you'd better not get confused with both terms, CRUD and REST are similar in terms of jargon."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research about the importance of CRUD in the context of web development. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write an article explaining how to use CRUD in the development of websites. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a glossary with the most important words related to CRUD in websites context. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read aloud your text to your class and interchange words and meanings in a dynamic way. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about the importance of CRUD in web development contexts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write accurate ideas about CRUD "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I recognize the vocabulary related to CRUD in websites context."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice my pronunciation in a dynamic way with my class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n5le01ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Teacher</b>: Ok, everybody, last class we talked about what CRUD was and today we're going to talk about CRUD in web development. So, let's see, Mary. Do you remember what CRUD is?</br>\n<b>Mary</b>: Sure, that's the short form of Create, Read, Update and Delete. But, I have a doubt teacher, do we really use CRUD when talking about web development?</br>\n<b>Teacher</b>: Well, sort of. In fact, when you talk about web development, you might want to refer to it not as CRUD, but REST.</br>"}, {"time": "34500", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>James</b>: Sorry, teacher. What does it stand for?</br>\n<b>Teacher</b>: It means Representational State Transfer, and once you manage CRUD, you're going to see that it is pretty similar to REST.</br>\n<b>Mary</b>: What is the difference, then?</br>\n<b>Teacher</b>: When we talk about databases such as MySQL, we talk about CRUD, but in terms of web development, REST is something deeper. It is an API that, in short, helps clients to exchange data with the servers via HTTP. </br>\n<b>James</b>: But, is it the same as CRUD?</br>"}, {"time": "73000", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><b>Teacher</b>: Guys, you'd better not get confused with both terms, CRUD and REST are similar in terms of jargon, I mean, within REST we'll find some commands like, GET PUT POST and DELETE which are somehow related to Create, Read, Update and Delete. In fact, they work similarly. Now, you ought to understand that such commands will work differently in web development. Those commands help the user to interact with websites; for example, when you post, request or delete a picture on a social media application. </br>\n<b>James</b>: Teacher, can we have some practice on that today?</br>\n<b>Teacher</b>: I'm afraid we won't do that as we're checking the theory today. In fact, you have that practice after next class. Today, you might want to open your books on page 45.</br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le01ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can briefly explain what CRUD means in the context of web development."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about how CRUD is used in the development of websites."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Which browser do you use when you surf the web? Why do you use that one? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you know what CRUD stands for? Share your thoughts. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "conten